From: Martin Kreichgauer <martinkr@google.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:38:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] [M156] [webauthn] Post FidoHidDevice error callbacks

Original change's description:
> [webauthn] Post FidoHidDevice error callbacks
>
> Because FidoDevice::DeviceTransact forbids implementations from invoking
> the response callback synchronously (i.e., hairpinning), FidoHidDevice
> violated this contract when in State::kMsgError or State::kDeviceError
> by running pending callbacks inline inside Transition(). Callers such as
> Ctap2DeviceOperation::Start() assign to `this->token_` after
> DeviceTransact() returns, which caused a use-after-free write when a
> hairpinned error callback destroyed the owning FidoTask and operation.
>
> Post error callbacks asynchronously in FidoHidDevice::Transition() so
> DeviceTransact() never hairpins.
>
> Fixed: 567370135
> Change-Id: Ibd13065af4e25f4c5f263d97937c20a0315edf39
